  "description": "The environmental science major prepares students to be Christ's agents of renewal by working as stewards of God's good creation. Graduates of this program are prepared for entry-level jobs in a variety of environmental fields, including land and resource management and environmental consulting, and they are prepared for graduate study in applied, interdisciplinary science programs, such as natural resource management. Students take a set of common courses and choose either the natural resources track or the naturalist track.",
